# Environment / secrets — NEVER commit these
*.env
*.env.local

# Server-specific system prompt context (real names, aliases) — keep local.
#
# discord-bot/prompts/ is ordinary committed code now: the prompt templates the
# bot renders, baked into the image. Only the context file is host-local, and it
# lives on the bot_context volume beside the session store (LORE_CONTEXT_PATH),
# not here. The path below stays ignored so the pre-migration copy, and anything
# that recreates it, cannot be committed.
discord-bot/prompts/lore_context.md

# Large model files
*.gguf
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
.venv/
scripts/.venv/
# Local venv for running the proxy test suite outside the container
proxy/.venv-test/
# Trainer test venv — pytest/httpx/yaml only, deliberately no torch, so the
# handover logic can be tested without a CUDA install.
lora-training/.venv-test/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node (LibreChat dev, if ever needed)
node_modules/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo

# Docker
*.log

# LoRA training outputs (large)
lora-training/outputs/
lora-training/checkpoints/
lora-training/runs/
# Arbiter test venv — pytest/yaml only, no GPU or Docker access needed.
arbiter/.venv-test/
# Bot test venv — discord.py/httpx/pytest, so the lore package can be tested
# without building the image.
discord-bot/.venv-test/

# Bot runtime state.
#
# Lore thread transcripts have moved out of the repo entirely, to
# /mnt/storage/array/DiscordArchive/bot_context (see the discord-bot volumes in
# docker-compose.yml) — they hold verbatim server history and every excerpt a
# /lore run retrieved. The path below stays ignored so the pre-migration copy,
# and anything that recreates it, cannot be committed.
#
# threads.json is the thread->model registry. It has moved to the bot_context
# volume alongside the sessions, because living inside the working tree meant a
# branch switch could (and did) delete it from under the running container. The
# path below stays ignored so a stale copy cannot be committed if anything
# recreates discord-bot/data/.
#
# The *.tmp entry covers the atomic temp file the stores write before rename.
discord-bot/data/lore_sessions.json
discord-bot/data/threads.json
discord-bot/data/*.tmp
